WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.660
What’s good y’all?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:22.440
This week we shakin dem haters off with "The Fountainhead" by Ayn Rand.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.780
Howard Roark is da only bruh in his architecture school who wanna shake things up.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.080
Errybody else just a buncha by-the-book hacks who think building design gotta rep tradition.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.300
But Roark don’t flow with dat mess — he got his own vision and don’t give a damn what they think.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.600
Brotha keep it so real that the school expels his ass, straight up.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.760
So he head to New York and start workin for an architect named Henry Cameron.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though Cameron’s rep ain’t so hot among the big dawgs anymore,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.560
Howard think he's the trillest architect in the game.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.660
Meanwhile, Howard’s homie from school, Peter Keating, just got a job up at a swag architecture firm,

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.480
workin fo some famous rich dude named Guy Francon.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:07.080
Roark and Cameron always makin real dank-ass designs, but nobody really cares about inspired work,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.140
so they gotta keep on da hustle jus
to scrape by.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:16.940
Whereas dat scrub, Peter, is able to stack mad grands just by smooth-talkin peeps and designin em pretty

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.120
weak-ass buildings.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.260
Before you know it, dude becomes full partner — even though he accidentally murked a guy to get there!

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:27.820
Peter feel bad... but not when bad feels this good! Yeah!

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.680
Eventually, Cameron retires, and Roark try to do his own thang.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.440
But that don’t last long, cuz he just keep it so damn real with his customers —

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.020
tellin em he don’t give a sh*t bout what they want — it's his design o’ nuthin.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:47.760
Eventually, he gotta get down 'n dirty and start grindin hard at a granite quarry owned by Peter’s boss, Francon.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.720
Peter been busy too — busy creepin’ on Francon’s daughter, Dominique.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.560
Roark see Dom, and they start vibin each other.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.700
Then one night, Roark go to da phat crib she stayin at, and rapes her —

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.940
though she say later, maybe it was just what she wanted. That's what da book say.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:08.700
So, she try to find Roark lookin fo anotha go, but brotha dipped out to New York to design anotha building.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.900
Dominique ends up headin to the city too,

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.880
and finally figure out that Roark ain’t just some granite quarry hustler.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.780
As a girl who knows a thing or two about architecture, she thinks his work is off the chain.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.700
They start hookin up on the DL, but in her public life, she try to destroy Roark's career.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.280
Girl got a serious hater streak to her.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.600
But she ain’t da only one —

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.960
there be this writer dude named Ellsworth M. Toohey who tryna ruin Howard’s rep.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:40.460
All this mess cuz both of em can’t stand how he can stay so legit in a world full of posers and fakers.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.800
Toohey comes up with a plan to break Roark once and fo’ all:

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:49.760
he convinces some dumbass to hire Roark to build a temple and then sue him after he see what Roark built.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:56.700
Up in court, all da top dawgs of architecture roll up to dat stand, and they just run they mouths, talkin sh*t bout Roark.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:02.480
Dominique don’t say nuthin, but on da inside, she know Roark is da only real deal up in dat courtroom.

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:06.849
When Roark lose the case and end up cashed out on the struggle again, Dominique says,

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:12.360
”Man, f**k it! If I live in a world where
real people get sh*t on, and hacks get da good life,

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:18.060
then I’m just gonna do the worst damn thing I can think of. First, no more Roark booty calls on da reg.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.840
And second, I’m gonna marry that b*tchass, Peter Keating."

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.560
Later, Dominique meet this rich newspaper man named Gail Wynand.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.980
Dude so into Dom that he literally buys her from Peter.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.540
Wynand thinks Roark's work is really fly, so they become boys,

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.520
even though he don’t know nuthin bout what went down between him and his woman.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.600
Eventually Keating lose all his rep, and errybody start seein him for the tool he is.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:46.420
Boy gets one last shot at a housing project and realize he need Roark, if he gonna do it right.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.020
Roark agree to help a brotha out under two conditions —

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.200
Numba 1. They gotta do it his way, and

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.400
Numba 2. He stays anonymous.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.320
They shake on it, but later Roark find out dat they messed with his vision.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.920
So what does he do? He burns dat muthaf**ka down.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.940
Da whole damn country hatin on Howard now, but at this point, he jus used to it.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:09.680
Wynand finally step up and defends his bro in the newspaper.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.800
But when da heat comes down, and Wynand gotta choose between Roark or his business,

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:17.220
he like “Roark who?” and throws his ass under the bus.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.240
Seems like it’s all over for Roark,

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:25.100
but at the trial, he rocks the mic, sayin how important it is to be true to nobody else but yo self.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.440
The Jury lets him off, Roark and Dominique become a thing again,

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.880
and Wynand ask him to build one more building —

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:38.920
a building so tight it gonna rep all da noble things about mankind.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:44.360
When it comes to keepin it 100 all day erry day, it jus don’t get no realer than Howard Roark.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:49.900
Matta fact, Rand say da reason she wrote dis book was to portray the most legit man you could think of —

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.680
one dat completely reppin her homebrew philosophy called "objectivism."

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.740
"This is the motive and purpose of my writing; the projection of an ideal man.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.900
The portrayal of a moral ideal, as my ultimate literary goal, as an end in itself —

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:10.120
to which any didactic, intellectual or philosophical values contained in a novel are only the means."

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:17.260
Objectivism preachin a couple things like: logic, self-interest, capitalism, atheism, personal responsibility,

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:20.240
and as far as reality go — what you see is what you get.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.939
So that’s a tight philosophy 'n all, but
what does this look like in the flesh?

00:05:24.939 --> 00:05:28.779
Well first off — Roark go hard in the paint when it comes to his integrity.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:33.720
To this dude, keepin it real means dedicating your life to one idea, and everything —

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.860
what you think, what you do, all of it — gotta rep this idea.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:41.760
No matter how raw it get when the haters start hatin, he don’t budge an inch.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.660
Cuz stickin by that idea is what makes you you.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.700
Most people can’t roll like Roark, though.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:52.460
Erry single day, da world ask people to compromise their values, and most just let it slide —

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:55.680
bit by bit — til they ain’t nuthin left of
their self.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.980
"... they die with every day that passes. When you meet them, they're not what you met last.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:05.380
In any given hour, they kill some part of themselves. They change, they deny, they contradict —

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:10.740
and they call it growth. At the end there's nothing left, nothing unreversed or unbetrayed."

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:17.140
If bein true to yo self is numba 1, then you can’t be givin a sh*t bout what errybody else think, like dat boy, Peter.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:21.480
People like him spend they whole lives worryin bout how they look in other people’s eyes.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.500
To them, it don’t matter how things are, only how it seem.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:30.680
Wynand is even worse. He ain’t even trippin bout how errybody else see him — he want power over em.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.980
But brotha soon recognize dat if you spend all yo life tryna possess others,

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.370
it’s yo ass that ends up gettin owned.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:43.020
"[Wynand] walked at random. He owned nothing, but he was owned by any part of the city. It was right that the

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:48.280
city should not direct his way and that he should be moved by the pull of chance corners. Here I am, my

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:53.580
masters, I am coming to salute you and acknowledge, wherever you want me, I shall go as I'm told.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.400
I'm the man who wanted power."

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:59.700
But on the real — can somebody like Roark really exist in a world this crooked?

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:06.240
Well it sho ain’t easy when literally errybody — even yo so-called “homies” — tryna take you down.

00:07:06.249 --> 00:07:08.389
I mean, just look at these haters —

00:07:08.389 --> 00:07:12.649
Toohey messin with him cuz he want da world to know that ideals don’t mean nuthin,

00:07:12.649 --> 00:07:16.449
Dominique think da world is too much of a twisted place for him to exist,

00:07:16.449 --> 00:07:21.549
and Wynand, quite simply, thinks a dude as real as Roark just can't exist, period.

00:07:21.549 --> 00:07:26.720
Crazy thing is, it’s him who ends up breakin, when he try to live up to Roark's baller status.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.720
Sho, Roark's will, determination,
and heroism are all pretty clutch.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:36.040
But dat don’t mean it’s all good — there’s plenty of jacked up sh*t bout Rand’s philosophy, too.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.000
One of da worst things is da way Rand
talks bout pity:

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:44.820
"But this was pity — this complete awareness of a man without worth or hope, this sense of finality, of the not to

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:49.920
be redeemed. There was shame in this feeling — his own shame that he should have to pronounce such

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:56.140
judgement upon a man, that he should know an emotion which contained no shred of respect. This is pity,

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:00.960
he thought, and then he lifted his head in wonder. He thought there must be something terribly wrong with a

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.320
world in which this monstrous feeling is called a virtue."

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.320
Look, I don’t know what an “ideal man” would look like —

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.660
but I sho as hell know he wouldn’t say feelin sorry for others is bullsh*t —

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.480
or dat bein generous to others is fo b*tches.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.760
No matter who you are or where you come from,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.900
somebody along the way has helped you get to where you are.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.580
All OGs know that.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.180
Thanks for watching, y'all!

